// Work over several frames (language.md §6.18): a `@job fn` whose body runs a part a frame, to
// each `yield`. `f.start(...)` takes its owned parameters and makes a `Job<f>`;
// `job.resume(...)` takes its `borrow` and `mut` parameters, runs it to its next `yield` or its
// end, and says which (`Step`).

/// A job of the `@job fn` `F` (`Job<realize>`, from `realize.start(...)`): where it stopped, and
/// the locals it needs after that point. An owned value with no projections in it, which a
/// field of the program's state holds.
pub struct Job<F> {}

/// What a job's `resume` did: it stopped at a `yield` (its work for this frame), or it ran to
/// its end, and gave its result.
pub enum Step<R> {
    Yielded,
    Done(R),
}
